# BYTHERIM RP — tests

Run everything:

    cd rp
    node tests/run-all.js

One-time setup (jsdom is the only dependency):

    npm install jsdom

## What each suite covers

**no-duplicate-members.js** — fails if any object literal defines the same
method twice. JavaScript silently keeps the last one, so a stale copy
overrides working code with no error. This has caused three separate
"blank screen" bugs in this project; it needs no dependencies and runs
instantly, so run it after any large edit.

**league-stats.js** — simulates a regular season and checks team averages
(points, rebounds, assists, steals, blocks, turnovers, fouls, shot volume)
against real NCAA Division I ranges. Catches tuning changes that push the
simulation somewhere unrealistic.

**season-cycle.js** — plays three full seasons with offseasons. Catches
problems that only appear in later years: rosters draining or overflowing,
declared players re-enrolling, offseason stages stalling, rating drift.

**draft-and-save.js** — checks the NBA lottery produces real-world odds,
the mock draft is well formed (60 unique picks, better prospects going
earlier), and the save file stays bounded. That last check exists because
the save once stored every player twice — inside `players` and again
inside each team's roster — which pushed a five-season file near 100 MB.

## Adding a test

`harness.js` boots the sim against the real `ncaa.html` in a headless DOM:

```js
const { boot, playSeason, playOffseason, ok } = require('./harness');
const { Sim, window } = boot({ roster: csvString });   // omit a sheet to simulate it being down
await Sim.init();
await Sim.startNewGame();
await playSeason(Sim);
ok(Sim.state.ncaaDone, 'season finished');
```
